    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "gotcha. so basically u're saying the dialect itself is a red flag for the staff. if a caller uses this kind of non-standard English, should the trainees assume they're less educated or less capable of following a professional process? i'm trying to decide if we should label these specific patterns in the manual as \"low-level\" communication so the reps know what to expect from certain types of people.",
